schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: "Crypto Donation Platforms: What You Need to Know"
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: comparison
  summary: >-
    Orients a nonprofit to what crypto-donation platforms do (donor landing
    page, handling blockchain transactions, optional conversion to dollars,
    payout, tax receipts), surveys named options (The Giving Block, Infinite
    Giving, CryptoAltruists, plus Causes/Facebook giving, Binance Charity,
    Alchemy Pay), gives a what-to-look-for checklist (fees, supported coins,
    instant conversion, integration, support), and a getting-started flow
    (verify 501(c)(3) status, customize page, publish, promote).
  audience: nonprofit staff choosing a crypto-donation platform to onboard
  known_tensions:
    - holding-crypto-for-appreciation vs instant-conversion-to-avoid-volatility
  related_concepts:
    - crypto-donation-adoption-communication
  related_resources:
    - The Giving Block
    - Infinite Giving
    - CryptoAltruists
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/crypto-donation-platforms.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-620c0c65c46f
  source_lineage: crypto-donation-platforms.md
  notes: |
    # assessed-but-excluded
    - no independent verification of platform fee levels, supported-coin counts,
      or nonprofit-verification requirements beyond what the article itself
      states; treated as a directory-style overview, not fact-checked pricing.
